<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices rise on plant demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices rise on plant demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Thursday rose by 100-200 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on better demand from some processing plants, dealers said.</p>
<p>Business was dull and undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained bearish in very thin trade. Soyoil solvent was down by 300 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 100 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained bearish.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was down by $3 in export and was down by 500 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Soymeal yellow was $242-245 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $92-93 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,200-3,250 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition.</p>
<p>Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
